Fetch a launch day's weather, or read a weather file, as a profile of air and wind

Usage: hpr weather [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  open-meteo  Open-Meteo's forecast at a site, or its archive of past forecasts
  wyoming     A University of Wyoming balloon sounding: a station's latest before the launch
  gfs         NOAA's GFS forecast (0.25°, the whole Earth) at a site, from NOMADS
  rap         NOAA's RAP forecast (13 km, the contiguous U.S. and nearby Canada and Mexico) at a site, from NOMADS
  era5        An ERA5 pressure-level file (netCDF) read at a site and time
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Print one JSON document on standard output instead of text; errors too

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use color. Auto colors what goes to a terminal and heeds NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE. JSON output never has color
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  Fetch the forecast for a launch at Black Rock and save its profile:
      hpr weather open-meteo --latitude 40.865 --longitude -119.063 --time 2026-09-26T16:00Z -o profile.json
  Read a balloon sounding launched before it:
      hpr weather wyoming --station 72489 --time 2026-09-26T16:00Z

Guide: https://hpr.fusionspace.co/cli.html#hpr-weather
